WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.138
Recent works began to explain in-context learning,

00:00:03.218 --> 00:00:05.713
but each keeps only part of the picture.

00:00:05.793 --> 00:00:08.351
Some ignore the nonlinear self-attention,

00:00:08.431 --> 00:00:11.634
others replace the nonlinear MLP with a linear one,

00:00:11.714 --> 00:00:15.495
and most study linear regression rather than
classification.

00:00:15.575 --> 00:00:23.090
None can characterize how to train a model that
generalizes under a distribution shift between training and test data,

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:27.982
and none analyze how pruning a trained model
changes its in-context ability.

00:00:28.062 --> 00:00:33.517
Since practitioners routinely prune large language
models to save compute while hoping

00:00:33.597 --> 00:00:35.576
to keep their in-context skills,

00:00:35.656 --> 00:00:38.730
closing this theoretical gap matters in practice.
